    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1735">

                <pb facs="1109" n="993" xml:id="pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11D29/70.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your September 19. The Department has no objection to the reexamination of such
                    witnesses as may be readily available but could not consent to the presentation
                    of witnesses who have left Panama.</p>
                <p>Continue to urge upon the Government of Panama the necessity of bringing the
                    investigation to an early conclusion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
